# 17. KEYBOARD-FIRST OPERATION

This requirement is mandatory.

Desktop users must be able to start typing immediately when the screen appears.

They must NOT click any input field first.

Use a global keyboard listener.

Implementation pattern:

```tsx
useEffect(() => {
  const handleKeyboard = (event: KeyboardEvent) => {
    if (lockState !== "locked") return;

    if (/^[0-9]$/.test(event.key)) {
      event.preventDefault();
      inputDigit(event.key);
      return;
    }

    if (event.key === "Backspace") {
      event.preventDefault();
      removeLastDigit();
      return;
    }

    if (
      event.key === "Enter" &&
      digits.every(Boolean)
    ) {
      event.preventDefault();
      void submitPin();
    }
  };

  window.addEventListener("keydown", handleKeyboard);

  return () => {
    window.removeEventListener("keydown", handleKeyboard);
  };
}, [digits, lockState]);
```

Keyboard behavior:

```text
number → enter digit
Backspace → remove previous digit
Enter → submit when six digits exist
```

